course: dictionary
lesson: 10280
title: Words that hurt
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Torment can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (a doing word). As a noun, it means great pain or suffering, or a person or thing that causes it. As a verb, it means to make someone suffer badly, or to tease or annoy someone on purpose, again and again.
explain: Use the context to choose the meaning. «Hurting or tormenting an animal is cruel, it can make the animal attack, and it is against the law.» Here tormenting is a doing word: someone is causing the animal pain on purpose. The clues cruel and against the law show it is serious, not just a bit of teasing.
explain: In everyday talk, «stop tormenting your sister» means stop teasing her again and again. Stories use the word for deep suffering, such as a bully who torments younger children. Ask yourself: is someone in pain, or is someone being teased on purpose?
fact: Torment is a noun and a verb: a torment, or to torment someone.
fact: «Torment» (noun) means great pain or suffering, in body or mind.
fact: «Tormented» means made to suffer badly, or teased and annoyed again and again.
fact: Tormenting an animal is cruel, is never allowed in school, and is against the law.
fact: Useful phrases: «in torment» means in great pain, «torment someone» means cause someone suffering, and «tormented by» means badly troubled by something.
exercise: «Hurting or tormenting an animal is cruel.» What does tormenting mean here? | Walking a dog in the park | Feeding a pet every day | *Causing pain or suffering on purpose | Giving an animal a warm bath
exercise: «Stop tormenting your sister.» What does this mean? | Tell her a secret | Help her with her homework | *Stop teasing her again and again | Stop playing with her toys
exercise: In a story, a bully torments younger children. What kind of word is torments here? | A word for a place | *A doing word | A describing word | A joining word
test: «She was in torment after the fall.» What does in torment mean? | Sitting down | In a hurry | *In great pain | Very happy with the best news
test: «The bully's teasing was a torment to the new girl.» What kind of word is torment here? | *A thing that causes great suffering or annoyance | A kind of sport | A name for a school | A doing word
exam: Which statement is true, according to the lesson's sentence? | It makes the animal happy | It is a fun game for the whole class | *Tormenting an animal is cruel and against the law | It is allowed on the school playground
